# Shell scripts and their bats tests run on Linux (the CI runner, the WSL host, and the containers the
# tests bind-mount this checkout into), so they must have LF endings in the working tree. Without this,
# core.autocrlf=true on a Windows checkout turns them into CRLF and bash fails on them
# ("set: pipefail: invalid option name"), which breaks the pre-push test run.
*.sh   text eol=lf
*.bats text eol=lf
